                ("Short message structure and object pronouns", "A practical message often gives the purpose first, then the key detail, then a request. In familiar exchanges, me/te/le/la can refer back to a known person or thing: « Je te préviens. »", [("Je te préviens : le rendez-vous est déplacé.", "Just to let you know: the meeting has been moved."), ("Merci de me confirmer l'heure.", "Please confirm the time for me.")]),
