                ("Because, so, and despite", "Use parce que to give a reason, donc to show a result, and malgré + noun to mark a contrast. Keep the sequence of events clear.", [("Le bus était en retard, donc nous avons pris le tram.", "The bus was late, so we took the tram."), ("Malgré le retard, nous avons passé une bonne journée.", "Despite the delay, we had a good day.")]),
